@CathieDWood says it is not a law but an artifact of how many technology platforms are compounding at once. The Industrial Revolution ran on three and took growth up fivefold, from 0.6% to 3%. We have five today, and artificial intelligence (AI) is the biggest catalyst of all of them.

The International Monetary Fund (IMF) still projects 3.1%.

